  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will use your knowledge of geometric patterns to create tables and graphs that will represent the area of a garden.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Create drawings, tables, and graphs that represent the area of a garden.</item>
  <item> Recognize a situation represented by a graph that increases and then decreases.</item>
</list>
<para>Here are th <emphasis>ctivities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item> 7.1.1: Noticing New Patterns of Change</item>
  <item> 7.1.2: The Relationship Between Length and Area</item>
  <list>
    <item> 7.1.2: Self Check</item>
    <item> 7.1.2: Additional Resources</item>
  </list>
  <item> 7.1.3: Plotting Measurements</item>
  <list>
    <item> 7.1.3: Self Check</item>
    <item> 7.1.3: Additional Resources</item>
  </list>
  <item> 7.1.4: The Input and Output of a Function</item>
</list>
<para>After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list>
  <item> 7.1.5: Practice</item>
  <item> 7.1.6: Lesson Summary</item>
</list></section>
</content>
</document>
